course: dictionary
lesson: 15368
title: Sovereignty: who makes the rules?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sovereignty is a big word, but it has a simple idea at its heart. A country has sovereignty when it has the full right and power to govern itself, with no other country controlling it. «Every country wants to make its own decisions about its schools and its laws.» That wish to decide for yourself is sovereignty.
explain: The word is often used with other words. «National sovereignty» means a nation's right to govern itself. «Respect sovereignty» means letting another country make its own choices. «Ukraine fights to protect its sovereignty» means Ukraine wants to keep control of its own land and government.
explain: Sovereignty also means supreme power. A king, a queen or a government can have sovereign power over a land. In the UK, «parliamentary sovereignty» means that Parliament makes the final laws. Use the context to decide which meaning fits: is the sentence about a country's freedom, or about who holds the power?
fact: Sovereignty means the full right and power of a country to govern itself.
fact: «Sovereignty» can also mean the supreme power of a king, queen or government over a land.
fact: The UN Charter says countries should respect each other's sovereignty and borders.
fact: «Parliamentary sovereignty» means Parliament makes the final laws in the UK.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Ukraine fights to protect its sovereignty.» What does sovereignty mean here? | A type of weather that lasts for a long time | The number of people who live in a town | A game played with a ball | *The full right of a country to govern itself without another country controlling it
exercise: «The UN Charter asks countries to respect each other's sovereignty and borders.» What should countries do? | *Let each other govern themselves and keep to their borders | Hide their borders from each other | Ignore each other's borders | Take control of each other's laws
exercise: «In the UK, parliamentary sovereignty means Parliament makes the final laws.» According to this sentence, who makes the final laws? | The weather forecaster | *Parliament | Every shop owner in the town | The school head teacher
test: What does the phrase «respect sovereignty» ask a country to do? | Hand over its king to another land | Ignore its neighbours completely | Copy the laws of other countries | *Let other countries govern themselves without interfering
test: Which of these means the supreme power over a land? | A school council choosing a class trip | The local football club | A farmer's field of wheat | *The king, queen or government that rules the land
exam: Which sentence uses sovereignty correctly? | She ran sovereignty around the park before school | The sovereignty was very tasty for lunch | Sovereignty is the colour of a summer sky | *The country wanted to keep its sovereignty and make its own laws
